@startuml
title SD Host Controller - Block Gap Request Timing Diagrams

skinparam defaultFontName Monospaced
skinparam defaultFontSize 11

legend top
  Figure 3-28: Stop At Block Gap Request is Not Accepted at the Last Block of the Read Transfer
  Figure 3-29: Continue Read Transfer by Continue Request
endlegend

|Figure 3-28: Stop At Block Gap Request NOT Accepted at Last Block|

concise "DAT line" as DAT1
concise "Read Wait" as RW1
concise "Stop At Block Gap Request (Control)" as SABGR1
concise "Continue Request (Control)" as CR1
concise "DAT Line Active (Status)" as DLA1
concise "Read Transfer Active (Status)" as RTA1
concise "Block Gap Event (Interrupt)" as BGE1
concise "Transfer Complete (Interrupt)" as TC1

@0
DAT1 is "Block N-2"
RW1 is low
SABGR1 is low
CR1 is low
DLA1 is high
RTA1 is high
BGE1 is low
TC1 is low

@100
DAT1 is "Block N-1"

@200
DAT1 is "Last block"

@250
SABGR1 is high
note bottom of SABGR1 : Set during last block\n(Request NOT accepted)

@350
DAT1 is idle
DLA1 is low
RTA1 is low

@380
TC1 is high
note bottom of TC1 : Transfer Complete generated\n(Block Gap Event NOT generated)

@400
SABGR1 is low
note bottom of SABGR1 : Driver clears if\nBlock Gap Event not set

|Figure 3-29: Continue Read Transfer by Continue Request|

concise "DAT line" as DAT2
concise "Read Wait" as RW2
concise "Stop At Block Gap Request (Control)" as SABGR2
concise "Continue Request (Control)" as CR2
concise "DAT Line Active (Status)" as DLA2
concise "Read Transfer Active (Status)" as RTA2
concise "Block Gap Event (Interrupt)" as BGE2
concise "Transfer Complete (Interrupt)" as TC2

@0
DAT2 is "Block N"
RW2 is low
SABGR2 is high
CR2 is low
DLA2 is high
RTA2 is high
BGE2 is low
TC2 is low

@80
DAT2 is "Gap"
RW2 is high
note bottom of RW2 : Read Wait asserted\nduring block gap

@100
DLA2 is low
RTA2 is low

@120
BGE2 is high
note bottom of BGE2 : Block Gap Event generated

@150
CR2 is high
note bottom of CR2 : Continue Request set\n(Stop At Block Gap = 0)

@170
RW2 is low
note bottom of RW2 : Read Wait released

@180
DLA2 is high
RTA2 is high
CR2 is low
note bottom of CR2 : Auto-cleared

@200
DAT2 is "Block N+1"

@300
DAT2 is "Last block"

@400
DAT2 is idle
DLA2 is low
note bottom of DLA2 : Clear without\nBlock Gap Event

@420
RTA2 is low
TC2 is high
note bottom of TC2 : Transfer Complete

@enduml